-- World Map: descriptions for the 18 POIs that had none, from the opening of each entry in the
-- "UPDATED Official Reference" doc (SOTERIA: POINTS OF INTEREST). Only empty descriptions are filled; safe to run twice.
-- Rimehollow is left empty: the doc has only its tagline ("Rootwraught settlement").
update public.locations l set notes = v.notes
from (values
  ('ANCIENT MAZE', 'The Ancient Maze is not but a foundation in the middle of the otherwise barren wastes. It is said to be marked by the dead. Located at the heart of the Brivihan Plains, the Ancient Temple stands tall and proud. Despite its deserted appearance, it emanates an aura of mystery and power that can be felt by anyone who approaches its ancient walls. The only visible entrance is a pair of imposing rock stairs that lead down into the depths of the dungeon below.'),
  ('BA''ELNIM''S RESTING PLACE', 'Ba''elnim''s Resting Place, a celestial marvel enshrined in the heart of the Ba''elnari civilization, is a sacred sanctuary believed to be the physical embodiment of Ba''elnim, the revered deity of light and wisdom. Towering spires of ethereal crystal pierce the skies, emanating a radiant glow that illuminates the surrounding landscape for miles around.'),
  ('BROKEN CATHEDRAL', 'Once a grand cathedral, this ancient structure is now a decaying ruin, its original splendor faded after ages of conflict. Yet whispered legends say it still holds concealed treasures and forgotten secrets appealing to explorers and treasure hunters brave enough to face its dangers. The interior of the Broken Cathedral reveals a somber tableau of decay and desolation. Dilapidated pews, covered in layers of dust and cobwebs, stand as silent witnesses to a congregation lost to history.'),
  ('DARK ELF CAMP', 'The Dark Elf compound established within the ancient Chronolithe ruins on the other side of the continent is known as "Shadowmire Enclave."'),
  ('DUNGEON OF THE DRAGON POOL', 'This perilous underground labyrinth once housed an ancient dragon. Now it is filled with traps, treasure, and monsters lurking in its twisting tunnels. At its heart lies the mystically-powered Dragon Pool. Inside, the dungeon unfolds as a sprawling network of dark and winding tunnels, caverns, and chambers. It is teeming with dangerous traps, arcane puzzles, and monstrous creatures lurking in the shadows.'),
  ('ELVEN RUINS', 'Stepping into the heart of the Elven Ruins, one can sense the lingering echoes of a forgotten alliance. These ancient ruins scattered throughout Sylvan Grove once belonged to a forgotten Elven kingdom of Ilothyr. Murals and relics found amidst the crumbling structures tell a story of unity and cooperation between the Elves and Dark Elves, revealing that the two races were once allies with shared knowledge and destinies.'),
  ('EMBRELYN', 'Major coastal trade hub and center of arts/culture, located south of the Chronolithe Wastes. Recently facing undead threats. The Graveyard to the east has been cropping up undead citizens who are plaguing the city at night. The city is ruled by a democratically elected council, and the citizens are actively involved in shaping the city''s future.'),
  ('EYMONT', 'Eymont, a resilient Telrok Orc-Elf camp, stands resolute amidst the rugged expanse of Kul’Kal Rakhar, a land traditionally dominated by the Kul’Kal Rakhar Orcs. Nestled deep within the untamed wilderness, Eymont is a testament to the Telrok’s fortitude and adaptability in a harsh environment.'),
  ('GATEWAY TO THE WASTES', 'A narrow mountain pass that serves as the one safe route for traders/travelers to enter or exit the barren Chronolithe Wastes. Bandits and beasts stalk its remote trails.'),
  ('GOLGOTHA PASS', 'The only known pass that connects the Corren Range to Sylvan Grove. The Corren Mountain Range is largely considered unpassable by most forms of travel. A treacherous high mountain pass with slick, narrow trails. Prone to avalanches and rockslides, it is a dangerous crossing, made more perilous by bands of ogres that ambush travelers in the Golgotha Pass''s sheer cliffs.'),
  ('JACK RED-LOCK BAY', 'Infamous for piracy and roguish pursuits, this stronghold was once led by the notorious Captain Jack Red-Lock. His lucrative exploits became legend across the islands. But later in life, seeing his legacy inspire cruelty, Red-Lock faked his death and retired secretly to a cove on Verdelie''re''s distant shore, leaving his fearsome reputation behind. Only a few loyal confidants know the truth.'),
  ('NEW HARSTEN', 'New Harsten is a bustling trade city located on the eastern coast of Veridora. It sits at the end of the Northern tip of the Corren Mountain Range and separates the two regions of the Brivihan Plains and the Falorn Fjords. It is known for its diverse population of humans, dwarves and elves, its vibrant markets and its skilled craftsmen.'),
  ('RED-LOCK''S SHIPWRECK', 'The shipwreck on the edge of Soteria''s continent of Beranthes is a haunting reminder of the past. Once a vessel owned by the infamous pirate known as Jack Red-Locks, it has now succumbed to the treacherous waters of the region. The ship is partially submerged, with its masts and rigging protruding from the water, rusted and deteriorated from years of exposure to the harsh sea. The hull of the ship is heavily damaged, with holes and cracks visible along its surface.'),
  ('STEEL COAST', 'The Coast is riddled with old artifacts, serving as remnants of a world forgotten. The Steel Coast is a long stretch of beach that runs along the Chronolithe Wastes. The name "Steel Coast" comes from the fact that the beach is littered with remnants of ancient technology from a long-lost civilization.'),
  ('THE OLD LAGOON', 'Surrounded by dense forest, the expansive Old Lagoon is inhabited by exotic creatures like sea serpents and mermaids. Legends say pirates buried treasure here long ago, though its purported location is guarded by a powerful sea witch.'),
  ('THE RUINS OF SZAR', 'On the southeastern shore of the Brivihan Plains, set in the rugged coastal cliffs and overlooking the vast expanse of the ocean, lies an enigmatic place known as the Ruins of Szara. This ancient site exudes an air of mystery and intrigue, whispering tales of forgotten civilizations and lost secrets. As the waves crash against the rocky shore and the wind carries whispers of forgotten lore, the Ruins of Szara beckon the curious and the brave.'),
  ('THETIS', 'Thetis, the majestic capital city of the Nazari, stands as a breathtaking monolithic marvel, half submerged in the crystal-clear waters of Velshroud Sea and half rising proudly above its shimmering surface.'),
  ('WITHERED DRAKE SIGHTING', 'A decaying dragon corpse found in the outskirts of the Lowlands, the withered drake is a foreboding sign. Its contorted skeletal remains and tattered wings suggest an unnatural death, giving credence to rumors that something sinister may lurk in the remote wilderness.')
) as v(name, notes)
where l.campaign_id is null and l.name = v.name and coalesce(btrim(l.notes), '') = '';
